{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014Y1xmBcyQivVSENq8TUWmE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Skill Foundry â€” Description\n2\t\n3\tThe Skill Foundry (`C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry`) is the single authoring home for John's\n4\tskills. It owns each skill's source of truth, declared in `map.json`, and pushes\n5\t**one-way** to `skills-master` (and from there to the Claude / Gemini / OpenClaw\n6\thosts) via `bin/sync-to-master.ps1`. `bin/check-map-drift.py` enforces that every\n7\tdelivered target still matches its Foundry source.\n8\t\n9\tThe remaining consolidation is being completed wave-by-wave with the **Foreman**\n10\torchestrator. The ground-truth gate for every wave is the pytest invariant suite\n11\t`tests/test_foundry_invariants.py`, which only **grows** as waves land\n12\t(anti-test-weakening).\n13\t\n14\t**Single-repo constraint.** Foreman commits within ONE git repo and gates on real\n15\tpytest. So Foreman does the Foundry-INTERNAL half (stage assets in, add governance\n16\tdocs, extend the invariant suite). The cross-repo half â€” repointing external refs,\n17\tdeleting sources in other repos, running the sync, publishing â€” is done MANUALLY as\n18\tthe `FINALIZE` steps in the plan, because it spans git boundaries (Foreman's\n19\trepo-boundary guard would HALT on it).\n20\t\n21\tFull rationale: `C:\\dev\\Skill-Foundry-Foreman-Plan-20260603.md`.\n22\tNarrative build history: `C:\\dev\\Skill-Foundry-Execution-Log.md`.\n23\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f0ca24c-ba7f-4cc1-ac6a-0896349e09d4","uuid":"fda20bc9-297e-485a-86d3-60d4c20a60c9","timestamp":"2026-06-19T04:53:20.723Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\DESCRIPTION.md","content":"# Skill Foundry â€” Description\n\nThe Skill Foundry (`C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry`) is the single authoring home for John's\nskills. It owns each skill's source of truth, declared in `map.json`, and pushes\n**one-way** to `skills-master` (and from there to the Claude / Gemini / OpenClaw\nhosts) via `bin/sync-to-master.ps1`. `bin/check-map-drift.py` enforces that every\ndelivered target still matches its Foundry source.\n\nThe remaining consolidation is being completed wave-by-wave with the **Foreman**\norchestrator. The ground-truth gate for every wave is the pytest invariant suite\n`tests/test_foundry_invariants.py`, which only **grows** as waves land\n(anti-test-weakening).\n\n**Single-repo constraint.** Foreman commits within ONE git repo and gates on real\npytest. So Foreman does the Foundry-INTERNAL half (stage assets in, add governance\ndocs, extend the invariant suite). The cross-repo half â€” repointing external refs,\ndeleting sources in other repos, running the sync, publishing â€” is done MANUALLY as\nthe `FINALIZE` steps in the plan, because it spans git boundaries (Foreman's\nrepo-boundary guard would HALT on it).\n\nFull rationale: `C:\\dev\\Skill-Foundry-Foreman-Plan-20260603.md`.\nNarrative build history: `C:\\dev\\Skill-Foundry-Execution-Log.md`.\n","numLines":23,"startLine":1,"totalLines":23}}}
